#: 593a193763b043169f280a413f35c803
msgid "**pin1**: power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:101
#: 31c8c02c324040059cd83dc1dd343986
msgid "**pin2**: TX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:102
#: 5c45f7900b4648c680bc937bab111914
msgid "**pin3**: RX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:103
#: 647f6d2b000e4922945d736f66ab61be
msgid "**pin5**: GND"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:105
#: 7e54d95857d44357811d2126ac6938b5
msgid "The 4 ports are called **/dev/tty-1**, **/dev/tty-2**, **/dev/tty-3** and **/dev/tty-4**. The first port is the one closest to the USB3 connector. The ports proceed counter-clockwise from there. So tty-2 is the one closest to the power connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:110
#: d43c41cd53eb45b3b3ad2323cb2475f5
msgid "The *default assignment* of the ports is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:112
#: a8c4362659c245d4916dc891130b75bb
msgid "**/dev/tty-1**: RC input (Spektrum satellite only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:113
#: 30e2fb75b515487cad3c9fb6e2a7e323
msgid "**/dev/tty-2**: telemetry at 57600"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:114
#: fb7d646868a5447bae3953a5b0175b32
msgid "**/dev/tty-3**: RC output (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:115
#: c7dfddbb622848cca5b259a733f126ea
msgid "**/dev/tty-4**: GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-qualcomm-snapdragon-flight-kit.rst:117
#: 810fbc484145472094386eeb596ce4b4
msgid "3 of the 4 ports provide 3.3V power on **pin1**, while the **/dev/tty-1** provides 5V power (note that **pin6** is not ground, unlike on a Pixhawk). You will need to check whether your GPS can be powered off 3.3V. A uBlox GPS is recommended, although any ArduPilot compatible serial GPS can be used."
msgstr ""

